# Validation_LightPipeCAD.mac — the light pipe in cad mode: the bundled ASCII STL
# box, 2000 Planck photons. Checks that CADMesh import runs clean under the
# invariants (no photon inside the wall, every termination labelled).
# The STL path comes from BBRSIMDATA (either env script sets it; the runner
# sources the installed one): /control/getEnv copies it into the alias
# {BBRSIMDATA}. Without it the macro stops at UIMAN0123 and writes no output.
# data/cad/box_sample.stl is a solid 40 x 40.7 x 10 mm box with a corner at the
# origin; the 1 x 7 x 7 mm emitter at x = -51 mm sits 50.5 mm upstream of its
# -x face, so no photon starts inside it (LP002 is checked in parametric mode
# only).
#
# Validate:
#   conda run -n bbrsim python <repo>/validation/check_invariants.py output/bbr.root
/run/verbose 0
/control/getEnv BBRSIMDATA
/bbr/lightpipe/mode cad
/bbr/lightpipe/stlPath {BBRSIMDATA}/cad/box_sample.stl
/bbr/thermal/emitterCenter -51 0 0 mm
/bbr/thermal/emitterSize 1 7 7 mm
/run/initialize
/random/setSeeds 11 13
/run/beamOn 2000
